.TH INSTALL-VSCODIUM 1
.SH NAME
install-vscodium \- install VSCodium through an official package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B install-vscodium
.RI [ --install ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints a dry-run installation plan by default. On Linux it selects the Flathub Flatpak package com.vscodium.codium; on Windows it selects the Winget package VSCodium.VSCodium; on macOS it selects the Homebrew cask vscodium. The helper invokes no installer unless --install is supplied.
.SH SAFETY
The helper does not bundle or redistribute VSCodium binaries. Package-manager signatures, source trust, license terms, and platform compatibility remain the responsibility of the configured upstream provider. It does not hide compatibility or emulation requirements.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a valid plan or successful installation command; 2 when the host or package manager is unsupported; otherwise the package manager's nonzero status.
